title: Upgrade and rollback
---
sequenceDiagram
  %% Source for 17-upgrade-rollback-flow.html. Edit this file, then run ./scripts/render-diagrams.py.
  %% Directives: docs in diagrams/README.md (Updating diagrams).
  %% @subtitle Compatibility check, rollback point, regression suite, and the two rollback modes
  %% @type security: CHK
  %% @type database: STATE
  actor OP as Operator
  participant CHK as Compatibility check<br/>isolated, read-only
  participant STATE as upgrade-state/<br/>images · checksums · backup
  participant ST as LiteLLM proxies
  participant V as verify-litellm-upgrade.py
  participant RB as rollback-litellm-upgrade.py

  OP->>CHK: candidate tag@digest
  alt not compatible
    CHK--xOP: keep the current image
  else compatible
    CHK-->>OP: compatible
    OP->>STATE: capture images, checksums, and a backup
    OP->>ST: update digests and recreate the proxies
    OP->>V: run the regression suite
    V->>ST: check every component
    alt all checks pass
      V-->>OP: upgrade complete
    else a check fails
      V--xOP: nonzero exit
      alt prior image reads the current schema
        OP->>RB: rollback --mode image-only
      else schema migrated incompatibly
        OP->>RB: rollback --mode restore-db
      end
      RB->>STATE: validate checksums and drift
      RB->>ST: restore the prior images and data
      RB->>ST: check proxy liveliness
      RB-->>OP: rolled back, report written
    end
  end
